"""Curated handover only: no credentials, raw sources or customer-linked exports."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,shutil,hashlib
import pandas as pd
import nbformat
from scripts.build_supervisor_model_review import execute,export_html

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
OUT=ROOT/'outputs/submission/20261018/CP2_Submission_Pack'

def main():
    OUT.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
    for source,destination in [('planning/CP2_FINAL_REPORT_DRAFT.md','01_Project_Report.md'),('planning/CP2_DEMO_GUIDE.md','02_Demonstration_Guide.md'),('planning/CP2_COMPLETION_STATUS.md','03_Completion_and_Limitations.md')]:shutil.copy2(ROOT/source,OUT/destination)
    docs=OUT/'Model_Evidence';docs.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
    for folder,name in [('20261017_larger_frozen_test','Larger_Frozen_Model_Test'),('20261017_calendar_free_notes','Calendar_Notes_Test'),('20261017_outcome_label_audit','Outcome_Label_Audit')]:
        for suffix in ['.html','.ipynb']:shutil.copy2(ROOT/'outputs/model_validation'/folder/(name+suffix),docs/(name+suffix))
    md=nbformat.v4.new_markdown_cell;code=nbformat.v4.new_code_cell
    partitions=[{'Part':'Training','Service dates':'8 Mar 2024–31 May 2025','Services':1506,'Returns':118},{'Part':'Validation','Service dates':'1 Jul–30 Nov 2025','Services':1177,'Returns':152},{'Part':'Assessment','Service dates':'1 Jan–27 Aug 2026','Services':2075,'Returns':184}]
    inputs=[{'Input group':'Service/package information','Examples':'Pest type, package size, service number, residential/commercial','Type':'Categories and numbers'},{'Input group':'Past recorded history','Examples':'Earlier services and return records known before prediction','Type':'Counts, time gaps, rates'},{'Input group':'Weather','Examples':'Earlier rainfall, temperature, humidity and soil moisture','Type':'Numbers'},{'Input group':'Location/environment','Examples':'Approximate location, mapped water/drainage, land cover','Type':'Numbers and missingness'},{'Input group':'Additional Calendar-note research','Examples':'Heavy/persisting/improving problem and treatment mentions','Type':'Ten binary mention flags; candidate only'}]
    def table(rows):return code('import pandas as pd\nfrom io import StringIO\n'+f'display(pd.read_json(StringIO({pd.DataFrame(rows).to_json(orient="records")!r})))')
    nb=nbformat.v4.new_notebook(cells=[md('# CP2 model review — start here\n\n**Question:** Will a matched paid service have a recorded pest-related return within 30 days?\n\n**Answer type:** yes/no classification with an estimated probability. The outcome is a Calendar return candidate; it is not automatically a formal warranty claim or confirmed biological recurrence.\n\n**Verdict:** experimental. We found some predictive signal but no consistently reliable replacement.'),md('## What inputs are used?\n\nThe frozen Extra Trees model uses **93 inputs: 87 numerical and six categorical**. It has 300 trees, maximum depth 10 and minimum leaf size five. Input count differs from the number of fitted tree nodes/parameters. Extra research inputs were tested separately; they were not silently added to the live model.'),table(inputs),md('## Why was the first test only 100 services?\n\nThat was a small held-out historical evaluation: five recorded return cases, two detected, three missed and three false warnings. Accuracy was 94%, below the 95% always-no-return baseline. The later final fit contains 5,695 services, so those training rows cannot be reused as unseen test records.\n\nA **separate model** was trained for a larger chronological test. The original frozen weights were preserved.'),table(partitions),md('June and December act as observation gaps. Property/programme groups were purged across partitions. The classifier was fitted on training only; validation selected calibration and the 0.14 threshold. No 2026 assessment tuning followed. The separate original model keeps its 0.19 threshold. Historical records and choices had already been explored, so this is not a completely fresh independent experiment.'),md('## Larger assessment result\n\nOn **2,075 services with 184 recorded returns**, the separate model detected **119**, missed **65**, and produced **398 false warnings**. Precision was **23.0%**, recall **64.7%**, F1 **34.0%** and accuracy **77.7%**. Always predicting no return gives 91.1% accuracy but detects none. These results show why accuracy alone is insufficient. Changing sample size does not automatically improve precision.\n\nThe original and larger tests used different fits/populations/thresholds; do not interpret the difference as the isolated effect of test-set size.'),md('## Did extra inputs help?\n\nCalendar-note inputs changed pooled F1 from **31.5% to 32.9%** on the same 2,172 validation services, but detected fewer returns. The period gains and probability errors were inconsistent. Weather between visits, weather before the first visit, stepwise selection, pest-specific history, team changes and historical food places also failed to establish a dependable replacement.\n\nA 40-window source audit found 19 positive windows supported by the confirmed warranty-booking rule, one complimentary return, and 20 negative windows with no recorded return. No definite error was established, but this stratified sample cannot establish population label accuracy.'),md('## What remains\n\nThe separately declared recovery experiment covers 16–30 October, with full outcome evaluation scheduled for **30 November 2026**. It must pass timely-prediction, complete-outcome, identity and integrity checks. Three source candidate flags remain documented; original gaps are not repaired after the event.\n\nThe report is complete with current historical evidence; the future addendum remains pending. The dashboard is owner work. General AI answers and approximate maps require source checking. No model performance guarantee is made.\n\nThis aggregate notebook contains no raw source exports. Its cells execute sequentially in Python and validate with nbformat. A native Jupyter kernel was unavailable for an additional execution check. The detailed evidence notebooks retain inspectable outputs; reproducing their original experiments requires the private project sources, which are deliberately not included.')])
    nb.metadata.kernelspec={'display_name':'Python 3','language':'python','name':'python3'}
    for cell in nb.cells:
        if cell.cell_type=='code':cell.metadata['jupyter']={'source_hidden':True}
    execute(nb);nbformat.validate(nb);nbformat.write(nb,OUT/'04_Model_Review.ipynb');export_html(nb,OUT/'04_Model_Review.html')
    evidence=json.loads((ROOT/'outputs/project_audit/20261018_completion/completion_summary.json').read_text())
    dbt=json.loads((ROOT/'outputs/project_audit/20261018_completion/dbt_reporting_scope_acceptance.json').read_text());evidence['reporting_dbt_tests_passed']=dbt['passed_selected_reporting_tests'];evidence['dbt_scope_note']=dbt['error_explanation']
    (OUT/'05_Verification_Summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(evidence,indent=2))
    (OUT/'READ_ME_FIRST.md').write_text('# CP2 current submission pack\n\nStart with 01_Project_Report.md. Use 04_Model_Review.html or its Jupyter notebook for the simple model explanation. 02_Demonstration_Guide.md is the presentation walkthrough. 03_Completion_and_Limitations.md explicitly lists the future evidence and owner dashboard work that are still pending.\n\nThis is a current handover, not a claim that the November prospective evaluation has completed. The model remains experimental. Detailed research files are in Model_Evidence. No credentials or raw customer exports are included. Do not upload the entire underlying project folder; it contains private sources.\n')
    inventory=[]
    for path in sorted(OUT.rglob('*')):
        if path.is_file() and path.name!='PACK_MANIFEST.json':inventory.append({'file':path.relative_to(OUT).as_posix(),'sha256':hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()})
    (OUT/'PACK_MANIFEST.json').write_text(json.dumps({'scope':'Curated current-evidence submission; November outcomes and owner dashboard pending','files':inventory},indent=2))
    archive=shutil.make_archive(str(OUT),'zip',root_dir=OUT.parent,base_dir=OUT.name)
    print(json.dumps({'pack':str(OUT),'zip':archive,'files':len(inventory)+1}))

if __name__=='__main__':main()
